          %p A very similar method establishes the following claim.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p Over ZF, AC is equivalent to the statement that every inhabited set admits a group structure.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p Every inhabited finite set admits a cyclic group structure, and under AC any infinite set can be put in bijection with the collection of its finite subsets, which forms a group under symmetric difference.
            %p
              Conversely, suppose
