            %em plump
            successor of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0
            the cardinality of the set of all
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 0
                    %mo +
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0^+ = \omega_1
            is the smallest
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uncountable+set"} uncountable
            ordinal. Assuming the axiom of choice (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
            and excluded middle are enough), we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 0
                    %mo +
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0^+ = \aleph_1
            as a cardinal.
          %p
            In general, we get a sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_\alpha
            of infinite cardinalities of well-orderable sets; assuming excluded middle, every infinite well-orderable cardinality shows up in this sequence. Assuming the axiom of choice, every infinite cardinal shows up, and we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ℵ
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\omega_\alpha| = \aleph_\alpha
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_0 = 0
            instead of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
